%N A123118 Partial products of A101695.
%C A123118 The number of prime factors (with multiplicity) of a(n) is T(n) = A000217(n) = n*(n+1)/2.
%F A123118 a(n) = Product_{i=1..n} i-th i-almost prime = Product_{i=1..n} A101695(i).
%e A123118 a(1) = 2 = prime(1).
%e A123118 a(2) = 12 = 2 * 6 = prime(1) * semiprime(2) = 2^2 * 3.
%e A123118 a(3) = 216 = 2 * 6 * 18 = prime(1) * semiprime(2) * 3-almostprime(3) = 2^3 * 3^3.
%e A123118 a(4) = 8640 = 2 * 6 * 18 * 40 = prime(1) * semiprime(2) * 3-almostprime(3) * 4-almostprime(4) = 2^6 * 3^3 * 5.
%e A123118 a(15) = 992421449860431053104969912494677242675200000 = 2 * 6 * 18 * 40 * 108 * 224 * 480 * 1296 * 2688 * 5632 * 11520 * 25600 * 53248 * 124416 * 258048 = 2^89 * 3^21 * 5^5 * 7^3 * 11 * 13.
